+            // gtel3g: the graphics HALs are deliberately NOT dumped here.
+            //
+            // dumpStackTraces() runs crash_dump32, which PTRACE_SEIZEs every
+            // thread of the target.  On this device crash_dump32 regularly
+            // fails to finish (it gets stuck in pipe_wait and is then reaped
+            // by its own alarm(30)), and because the stop was tracer-initiated
+            // __ptrace_unlink() leaves the tracee in group-stop -- it stays
+            // "t (tracing stop)" until something sends it SIGCONT.
+            //
+            // Freezing android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1-service is
+            // fatal: SurfaceFlinger's main thread blocks forever in
+            // executeCommands()/presentDisplay(), its binder threads pile up
+            // in getNewTexture(), and system_server's own main thread then
+            // blocks in SurfaceControl.nativeGetPhysicalDisplayIds().  That
+            // trips this very Watchdog, which dumps the HAL again, which
+            // freezes it again -- a permanent black screen with a
+            // system_server restart loop and a growing pile of unreapable
+            // crash_dump32 zombies.
+            //
+            // A diagnostic stack dump must never be able to wedge the display
+            // pipeline, so the composer and its allocator are excluded.
+            // "android.hardware.graphics.allocator@2.0::IAllocator",
+            // "android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1::IComposer",
